The hardware address to set on the interface in the network namespace.

When not set, the interface keeps the address the kernel gave it, a new one
at each start, except on a l2_bridge network: the address is then derived
from the id of the object and the id of the resource, locally administered,
the same at every start and on every node the object runs on. A dhcp server
of the segment can reserve an address for it, and the neighbors of a static
address keep the entry they learned. Each instance of a flex object has its
own, derived from the name of its node too.
